WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.729
This npm package

00:00:01.541 --> 00:00:02.861
installed an AI

00:00:02.673 --> 00:00:03.734
agent backdoor

00:00:04.254 --> 00:00:05.468
A fake CRM

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:06.636
client on npm

00:00:06.695 --> 00:00:08.735
called leadstack crm-connect

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:10.433
installed Hermes Agent

00:00:10.622 --> 00:00:11.895
an open-source AI

00:00:11.707 --> 00:00:12.402
agent

00:00:12.497 --> 00:00:13.428
and wired it

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:14.254
to the attacker's

00:00:14.065 --> 00:00:15.126
Telegram bot

00:00:15.646 --> 00:00:16.318
It ran as

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:17.202
a system service

00:00:17.155 --> 00:00:17.980
as root if

00:00:17.898 --> 00:00:19.077
npm install ran

00:00:18.889 --> 00:00:19.537
as root

00:00:19.676 --> 00:00:20.584
From a chat

00:00:20.608 --> 00:00:21.562
the attacker could

00:00:21.374 --> 00:00:22.636
run shell commands

00:00:22.671 --> 00:00:23.591
edit files

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:25.041
browse and schedule

00:00:24.853 --> 00:00:25.584
jobs

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:27.269
Nine versions went

00:00:27.081 --> 00:00:28.673
up on November 16

00:00:28.812 --> 00:00:30.156
SafeDep flagged it

00:00:29.967 --> 00:00:31.241
five minutes after

00:00:31.052 --> 00:00:32.007
the last release

00:00:31.819 --> 00:00:33.163
and npm removed

00:00:32.975 --> 00:00:33.328
it

00:00:33.493 --> 00:00:34.460
but the publisher

00:00:34.272 --> 00:00:35.439
is still active

00:00:35.958 --> 00:00:36.972
Full story on

00:00:36.783 --> 00:00:37.679
the dashboard
